KG42.register("source_edge_archive-ffd2dc315f8d3271845b193e",{"id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R001::E::v141-c-R001-E001","paper":"07-nash_bargaining","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","rule_ref":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R001","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R001-E001","source":"clearing.social_welfare","target":"clearing.inter_area","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-5931b196ea5babe4","target":"KG31-95bb253080ce87de","source_occurrence_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R001::V::clearing.social_welfare","target_occurrence_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-c-R001::V::clearing.inter_area","source_unit_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-a-M01::clearing.social_welfare","target_unit_id":"07-nash_bargaining::v141-a-M01::clearing.inter_area","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Day-ahead energy allocation among interconnected microgrids; P1 covers all microgrids in M. | Energy-allocation component of the virtual clearing-house service for interconnected microgrids at the beginning of daily operation. | Inter-microgrid allocations within each microgrid's power balance, for every microgrid and time slot. | Inter-microgrid energy allocations for every distinct microgrid pair and every time slot. | The P1 energy-allocation iteration in Step 1 of Algorithm 1.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e19","v141-b-g01-e20","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g02-E37"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"b2ff3aa842f3651e27084813747dbb8ec015416dff0a919400b963561df018c4","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"Economic objective and its applicability in this mechanism: P1 first minimizes interconnected microgrids total operating cost and fixes bilateral energy; P2 maximizes the product of net gains of the active trading set through payment bargaining.","target_definition":"P1 jointly minimizes operating cost across microgrids with local balances, storage/demand constraints and bilateral antisymmetry of exchanged energy. ADMM implementation and virtual clearing house do not turn this into contract-network matching or an auction.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Social operating cost minimization in P1 yields optimal energy scheduling and inter-microgrid energy allocations for all microgrids. Scope: Day-ahead energy allocation among interconnected microgrids; P1 covers all microgrids in M. Condition: P1 is solved subject to (1)–(3), (5), (6), (8)–(11), (14), (15), and (17).","expression":"\\min_{\\{g_i,q_i,x_n,r_{c,i},r_{d,i},e_i\\}_{i\\in\\mathcal{M}}} \\sum_{i\\in\\mathcal{M}} CO_i(q_i,x_n,r_{c,i},r_{d,i}) \\quad \\text{subject to } (1)\\text{--}(3),(5),(6),(8)\\text{--}(11),(14),(15),(17)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.social_welfare","clearing.inter_area"],"variable_refs":["x_g_i","x_q_i","x_x_n","x_r_c_i","x_r_d_i","x_e_i"],"parameter_refs":["theta_M"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-7e85444402-p06-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":"2652","section":"IV. PROBLEM ANALYSIS","anchor_text":"BP can be decomposed into two sequential subproblems on energy d- trading & scheduling and trading p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Theorem 1: The energy-trading bargaining problem NBP can be decomposed into two sequential subproblems on energy trading & scheduling and trading payment, denoted as P1 and P2, respectively. In the first step, we solve a social operating cost minimization problem P1 for the interconnected-microgrids system, which yields the optimal energy scheduling and energy trading for all microgrids. Those microgrids that trade energy with other microgrids form the set M′. In the second step, microgrids in set M′ bargain with each other to determine the energy-trading payments in P2."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-7e85444402-p06-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":"2652","section":"IV. PROBLEM ANALYSIS","anchor_text":"BP can be decomposed into two sequential subproblems on energy d- trading & scheduling and trading p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"P1: Social operating cost minimization problem:\nmin ∑_{i∈M} CO_i(q_i, x_n, r_{c,i}, r_{d,i})\nsubject to (1)–(3), (5), (6), (8)–(11), (14), (15), and (17),\nvariables: { g_i, q_i, x_n, r_{c,i}, r_{d,i}, e_i, i ∈ M }.\nSolving P1 determines the optimal energy trading & scheduling {g_i^*, q_i^*, x_n^*, r_{c,i}^*, r_{d,i}^*, e_i^*} for each microgrid i ∈ M. If a microgrid i has a nonzero energy trading vector e_i, then it belongs to set M′, and will participate in the payment bargaining in Problem P2. For the non-trading microgrids j ∈ M\\M′, they do not participate in the payment bargaining and their operating costs are the same as the disagreement points C_j^{Non}."}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Day-ahead energy allocation among interconnected microgrids; P1 covers all microgrids in M. | Energy-allocation component of the virtual clearing-house service for interconnected microgrids at the beginning of daily operation. | Inter-microgrid allocations within each microgrid's power balance, for every microgrid and time slot. | Inter-microgrid energy allocations for every distinct microgrid pair and every time slot. | The P1 energy-allocation iteration in Step 1 of Algorithm 1.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e19","v141-b-g01-e20","v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18","v141-b-g02-E35","v141-b-g02-E36","v141-b-g02-E37"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R001-E001","source":"clearing.social_welfare","target":"clearing.inter_area","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E17","v141-b-g02-E18"]},"paper_scope_note":"Distinguish the interfaces of P1 dispatch, P2 payment, the actual transaction set, and the clearing institution; the same clearing institution does not mean that the variables of P1 and P2 can be merged."}});
